# Installation

This plugin runs trusted code in the datalab API process{% if tool_ui_kind == "in-app" %} and
trusted JavaScript in signed-in users' datalab pages{% endif %}. Review the
selected release, dependencies, and built assets before installing it.

## Install in datalab

Add the plugin to the datalab checkout's root `plugins.toml`, preserving any
existing dependencies and source entries:

```toml
dependencies = [{{ distribution_name | tojson }}]

[tool.uv.sources]
{{ distribution_name }} = { git = "https://github.com/{{ repository_namespace }}/{{ repository_name }}.git", rev = "<reviewed-tag-or-commit>" }
```

Install the configured plugins:

```shell
cd pydatalab
uv run invoke dev.install
```

Restart a native datalab API, or rebuild and recreate its Docker images. Sign in
as a normal user and confirm that **{{ tool_name }}** appears under **Tools**{% if add_item_table_action %}
and that **{{ item_table_action_label }}** appears for a valid selection in the
configured item tables{% endif %}.

The generic datalab
[plugin operations guide](https://docs.datalab-org.io/en/latest/plugins/#installing-and-maintaining-plugins)
is the source for Docker behavior, upgrades, rollback, removal, and tool ordering
or disabling.

## Development setup

Install [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), then clone and check the project:

```shell
git clone https://github.com/{{ repository_namespace }}/{{ repository_name }}.git
cd {{ repository_name }}
uv sync --locked --all-extras --dev
uv run pytest
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

{% if tool_ui_kind == "in-app" %}
After changing the frontend, rebuild the bundle:

```shell
cd frontend
corepack yarn install --frozen-lockfile
corepack yarn build
cd ..
```

Commit `frontend/yarn.lock` and
`src/{{ distribution_name | replace('-', '_') }}/static/frontend/tool.js`.
{% endif %}

For integration testing, replace the Git source above with an editable path to
this checkout. Rerun `uv run invoke dev.install`, restart datalab, and exercise
the tool as a normal user.
